# Digest: <flow title>

> This is the operator-facing summary of a completed agent retro. The technical retro task remains the audit record. This digest is a plain-language reading surface: it should help the operator decide what deserves attention without opening the technical record.

> **Spec alignment (2026-08-08, source=t_5dc19cae):** This template is the canonical 10-section retro-digest fillable form, **Type 2 (Retro digest)** in the `executive-reporting` skill's 5-type taxonomy (`~/.hermes/skills/productivity/executive-reporting/references/per-digest-type-shape.md`). The canonical 8-section shape contract it specializes is in `methodology/03b-decide-operator-agent-interaction.md` Part 13; this template preserves all 8 canonical sections and adds 2 retro-specific sections — §4 "Council / agent agree and disagree" (between canonical §3 and §5) and §9 "Individual council / agent responses" (between canonical §5 and §6, with the per-seat detail at the bottom tier). The canonical 8-section fillable form for non-retro operator-review artifacts (Types 1, 3, 4, 5) is `~/.hermes/skills/productivity/executive-reporting/templates/executive-report.md.template` (the skill's counterpart to this template). v0.4.0 added the §4 agreement-column guidance (closes audit gap 3) and the §3 "Why it matters" sourcing guidance (closes audit gap 4) — see the HTML comments in §3 and §4 below.

**Reading guidance:** the operator reads top-down. Sections 1–3 are the **actionable top tier** — what this is, what matters, and what you need to do. Read them in 30 seconds. Sections 4–5 are the **transitional interpretation layer** — the council's overall disagreement structure and the substantive findings with proposed corrective actions. Sections 6–7 are the **operator action surface** — your decisions and your observations, in your own hand. Sections 8–10 are the **technical-detail bottom tier**, collapsed — evidence anchors, per-seat / per-axis individual responses, and digest metadata. **Technical detail belongs in sections 8–10, collapsed, expandable.** The single largest change vs v0.1.x: Individual council / agent responses was section 5 (middle) and is now section 9 (bottom tier), per the operator's 2026-08-08 direction (source=t_4d1de050). v0.3.0 added "Council content decisions (inline)" under section 3 + "Council content decisions (per-seat)" under section 9, so the operator can read and disposition content decisions without leaving the digest, per the operator's 2026-08-08 direction (source=t_9450b7e0).

