**Why it matters sourcing (v0.4.0, source=t_5dc19cae — closes audit gap 4):**
the "Why it matters" + "Consequence of not acting" copy MUST come from the
Retro-A task body's proposed corrective action for each finding. Do NOT use
stub strings from the verifier's `result` payload (e.g.
"(residual surfaced in Retro-A publish comment)" is a stub, not a real
reason). When the verifier's result is minimal, re-read the Retro-A task
body and extract the actual consequence. Per skill translation discipline
Rule 4 (translate severity into consequence) and Rule 5 (translate jargon
into outcome): the action items surface is plain-language consequence, not
the verifier's payload. The action items MUST satisfy the canonical 6
translation rules in `~/.hermes/skills/productivity/executive-reporting/
references/translation-discipline.md`.
-->

