## 4. Council / agent agree and disagree

<!--
Transitional interpretation layer. If a council deliberated, this section
shows the agree-vs-disagree table. The operator sees the structure of any
disagreement in 10 seconds. Include this section only when a council ran;
for single-agent retros, omit and replace with a one-paragraph "Direction"
statement.

Agreement column guidance (v0.4.0, source=t_5dc19cae — closes audit gap 3):
- "Unanimous (N/N)" — every seat's verdict matches the recommendation header.
- "Split (X-Y, <seat-names> dissented)" — at least one seat differs from the
  recommendation header; name the dissenting seats and show the count.
- The agreement column reflects the ACTUAL per-seat outcome (section 9), not
  the recommendation header. If section 4 says "Unanimous" but section 9
  shows a split, section 4 is WRONG. The verifier should spot-check this
  before marking ready.

Per skill translation discipline Rule 1 (preserve conclusions, replace
language): the conclusion is the actual agreement shape, not the
recommendation header. The digest reports the agreement shape; the
operator's decisions on the agreement live in section 6 (Operator decisions).
-->

| Question or axis | Council / agent position | Agreement |
|---|---|---|
| <Q1 or axis 1> | <recommendation> | Unanimous / Split (dissent named) |
| <Q2 or axis 2> | <recommendation> | Unanimous / Split (dissent named) |
| <Q3 or axis 3> | <recommendation> | Unanimous / Split (dissent named) |

**Direction:** <one-paragraph synthesis of where the council landed and where the open disagreements are, in plain language.>

